# expected.env — shape metadata of the legacy 2-PF patched NCCL (scripts/node/nccl/build.sh's
# build target), next to its authoritative sha in scripts/node/nccl/SHA256SUMS (the
# 'nccl-patched/libnccl.so.2' line). Sourced by build.sh, which compares a rebuilt library
# against all three and prints MATCH / DIFFERS for each.
#
# PRODUCTION SINCE 2026-10-10: the four-PF library ('nccl-patched-4pf/libnccl.so.2' line,
# sha 8de68def…, 61,426,528 bytes, 165 symbols — NCCL v2.30.7+cuda13.0, othexmr four-patch
# stack + the site listener patch, built by the NVFP4 recipe's site/nccl-4pf/build-4pf.sh).
# This legacy lib is the ROLLBACK artifact (keep both staged; never swap in place).
#
# A rebuild is NOT bit-reproducible (see scripts/node/nccl/README.md): the sha is expected to differ
# (the original 2026-09-01 build was 9bf76f03…, 61581272 bytes; the 2026-09-04 rebuild below is what runs now),
# while size and symbol count must stay in the same shape. A large deviation in either means
# the wrong gencode, the wrong base tag or a partially applied patch.
#
# Measured on rank 1 on 2026-09-04 14:00 from the rebuild made by scripts/node/nccl/build.sh (from-zero rehearsal), the very
# binary deployed as ~/nccl-patched/libnccl.so.2 on all 4 nodes.

# LEGACY 2-PF LIB SHAPE (the rollback artifact this script builds):
# stat -Lc %s libnccl.so.2
NCCL_EXPECTED_SIZE=61581280
# nm -D --defined-only libnccl.so.2 | wc -l
NCCL_EXPECTED_SYMBOLS=165
# Base tag and the commit the vendored patch applies to.
NCCL_TAG=v2.30.7-1
NCCL_COMMIT=73cf112295c33aee2b895f329f592f2a9b4b0f97
